<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-ABARE Australian crop forecasts for 1996/97.</title>
<headline>RTRS-ABARE Australian crop forecasts for 1996/97.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Bureau of Agricultural and Resource Economics (ABARE) issued the following forecast for Australian crops and areas for the 1996/97 season ending March 31, 1997, in its latest Crop Report, dated Feb 25.</p>
<p>Crops in million tonnes and areas in million hectares, with 1995/96 estimates for comparison:</p>
<p>			    Crop			 Area</p>
<p>		   1996/97    1995/96	1996/97   1995/96</p>
<p> Wheat	    23.50	16.98	  11.00	9.72</p>
<p> Barley	    6.08	 5.50	   3.26	3.20</p>
<p> Oats		1.62	 1.67	   0.91	1.04</p>
<p> Triticale	 0.54	 0.31	   0.30	0.18</p>
<p> Sorghum	   0.99	 1.56	   0.50	0.65</p>
<p> Maize	     0.31	 0.32	   0.07	0.06</p>
<p> Rice		1.46	 0.95	   0.16	0.15</p>
<p> Canola	    0.62	 0.56	   0.38	0.41</p>
<p> Lupins	    1.29	 1.43	   1.23	1.31</p>
<p> Cottonseed	0.79	 0.60	   0.40	0.30</p>
<p> Field peas	0.38	 0.47	   0.31	0.35</p>
<p> Chick peas	0.28	 0.26	   0.22	0.21</p>
<p>State wheat crop and area forecasts were:</p>
<p> Queensland	2.40	 0.56	   1.00	0.68</p>
<p> NSW		 8.00	 4.66	   3.00	2.48</p>
<p> Victoria	  2.80	 1.96	   1.05	0.90</p>
<p> S. Australia    2.80	 2.89	   1.60	1.61</p>
<p> W. Australia    7.61	 6.90	   4.35	4.05</p>
<p>State barley crop and area forecasts were:</p>
<p>  NSW		1.200	0.880	  0.530     0.570</p>
<p>  Victoria	 1.030	1.200	  0.610     0.680</p>
<p>  Queensland     0.450	0.190	  0.200     0.185</p>
<p>  S. Australia   1.900	1.900	  1.070     1.050</p>
<p>  W. Australia   1.460	1.300	  0.835     0.700</p>
<p>  Tasmania	 0.035	0.028	  0.013     0.012</p>
<p>(Any discrepancies are due to rounding)</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
